# Float ⇄ RGBA (IEEE754)
**Category:** Data Encoding/Decoding  
**Difficulty:** Beginner  
**Tags:** encoding, float, rgba, bitcast, screen-bus

Lossless packing of a 32‑bit float into RGBA8 and back. Useful when the screen (rgba8) is your storage medium.

```wgsl
// METADATA: Category=Data Encoding/Decoding, Difficulty=Beginner, Tags=[encoding,float,rgba,bitcast,screen-bus]
fn encode_float_to_rgba(value: f32) -> vec4<f32> {
  let bits: u32 = bitcast<u32>(value);
  return vec4<f32>(
    f32((bits >> 24u) & 0xFFu) / 255.0,
    f32((bits >> 16u) & 0xFFu) / 255.0,
    f32((bits >>  8u) & 0xFFu) / 255.0,
    f32( bits         & 0xFFu) / 255.0
  );
}
fn decode_rgba_to_float(c: vec4<f32>) -> f32 {
  let bits = (u32(c.r * 255.0) << 24u) |
             (u32(c.g * 255.0) << 16u) |
             (u32(c.b * 255.0) <<  8u) |
              u32(c.a * 255.0);
  return bitcast<f32>(bits);
}
```

